abstract: >-
  FluBNF forecasts weekly influenza hospital admissions for the 52 US
  jurisdictions of the CDC FluSight challenge. Its shipped forecast is an
  unfitted, equal-weight, quantile-averaged ensemble of two members: a
  sequential particle filter over an SIHRS compartmental model written in
  BNGL, fitted with a fork of PyBNF on the bngsim engine, and a calendar
  analogue whose donor pool excludes the calendar-inverted 2021-22 season.
  In a vintage-true retrospective of the 2023-24, 2024-25, and 2025-26
  seasons at full grid (15,460 scored cells), the ensemble scored a pooled
  weighted interval score of 0.678 relative to the CDC FluSight-baseline
  (ratio of WIS sums on shared cells; 0.813, 0.618, and 0.683 by season),
  beating the baseline in every season.
  All scores are self-computed from the hub's archived vintage data and
  baseline files, and are retrospective replays rather than real-time
  submissions. Reproducing the 2025-26 and pooled figures at printed
  precision requires the pre-fix analogue code state (repository commit
  9b0ef26; a calendar fix in commit 52cc22f, made after the record was
  sealed, moves them to 0.681 and 0.677 on current code), as recorded in
  docs/RELEASE-1.0.md.
